<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion, sweep, ablation, segmentation and rendering are separate functions. Six Lean theorems encode the shell-thickness window, the diffusion-ratio threshold, the integer margin, equal-diffusion failure, the successor egg length, and the Holocene single node. Lean was not run here." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script implements Schnakenberg kinetics, the Jacobian trace and determinant, sigma(k), and a diffusivity rescale that places the fastest mode on 10^(-2.929) m. Equal diffusion is predicted stable. The kinetics are the standard Schnakenberg form, not a feather-specific parameter table from Prum and Williamson." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Self-test on this run: dispersion lambda 1.1767 mm, PDE lambda 1.1685 mm, Pearson r 0.9979, RMSE 0.0301 mm, KS 0.143, pore FFT 0.663 mm against shell thickness 1.11 mm. n=7 for the KS sample is small. Values are not copied onto their references. Pass 1 holds the score at 80 until those numbers are the measurement record." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
