<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri — MorphoEval overall 81.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 overall 81.4. The dispersion law, ablation and specimen segmentation are implemented and the self-test reports r=0.9979, RMSE=0.0301 mm, ablation amplitude ratio 0.0039, photograph pore spacing 0.663 mm. Specimen-match stays at 72 because that pore spacing is not lambda_c and the first display scale hid the lattice. Overall 81.4/100 (faithfulness 79.4, reproducibility 86.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 95244113b1348dfeec9466cf094db251e2807d75; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/aptenodytes_forsteri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 95244113b1348dfeec9466cf094db251e2807d75, image/png, 259363 B, 1464×648 px, artifact_sha256 4a0ff4289fae61fc4874e6ee493314e76e29174e2b0d8d624c673cdf12806435 (sha256 4a0ff4289fae61fc4874e6ee493314e76e29174e2b0d8d624c673cdf12806435), spec_fingerprint 8258983b5a6bcf70e050b83d480003ff7d17bbb90cda5744e49bb2bec31fced1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8258983b5a6bcf70e050b83d480003ff7d17bbb90cda5744e49bb2bec31fced1; artifact_sha256: 4a0ff4289fae61fc4874e6ee493314e76e29174e2b0d8d624c673cdf12806435; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aptenodytes_forsteri_turing_wavelength_s0/aptenodytes_forsteri_specimen.jpg=70b89e84383c36f8...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather pigment patterns can be RD spots, bars, and dot arrays. | Chinese Journal of Polar Research 2008: emperor egg 121.3 by 83.8 mm, shell thickness 1.11 mm (0.94-1.32).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.20, b=0.30, D_v/D_u=42, with D_u set so the fastest mode is 10^(-2.929) m. | Commensurate-scale sweep comparing dispersion wavelength to the PDE Fourier peak.; transfer_boundary: Shell thickness is a through-shell length. Using it as the lateral wavelength is a scale identification for this tier, not a published pore-spacing measurement.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the MHNT photograph's 0.66 mm pore FFT equals lambda_c. | Does not claim body-scale black-white countershading is a 1.178 mm Turing mode. | Does not claim a predecessor chronospecies; the series length is 1. | Sibling slot 119 parameters (alpha 1.31) are not used.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Publish Pearson r, RMSE and KS for the commensurate-scale sweep, with law and PDE values not copied onto each other.",
        "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.5]: Equal-diffusion ablation and the scale sweep must be visible in the comparison figure, not only in the self-test log.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Segment the real MHNT egg and compare foreground, coherency and circularity to the simulated patch without setting value equal to reference.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=2.5]: Min-max colour scale collapsed the activator to one hot pixel. Rescale from the median to the 99.5th percentile so the spot lattice is visible, and keep the 0.66 mm pore measurement beside lambda_c." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.14e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Seven commensurate scale factors move the dispersion wavelength, and the PDE peak follows them. Setting D_u = D_v drops the amplitude ratio to 0.0039. The figure must still show that sweep and the ablation in the caption before this score is raised." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

